<body>

<div class="page">
  <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 40px;">
    <h1 style="font-size: 2.5em; margin: 0;">Publications</h1>
    <div style="text-align: right;">
      <span data-field="publication_year">{{ publication_year }}</span>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="content-grid">
    <!-- Column 1 -->
    <div class="book-entry">
      <img src="placeholder.png" alt="Book Cover" class="book-image">
      <div class="book-details">
        <h3><span data-field="title_1">{{ title_1 }}</span></h3>
        <p>EDITED BY <span data-field="editor_1_name">{{ editor_1_name }}</span>, <span data-field="editor_1_name">{{ editor_1_name }}</span> and <span data-field="editor_1_name">{{ editor_1_name }}</span></p>
        <p>The increasing worldwide trend in disasters, which will be aggravated by global environmental change (including climate change), urges us to implement new approaches to disaster risk reduction (DRR). This book provides a comprehensive overview of the DRR concept, its evolution, and the various approaches to disaster risk reduction (DRR) is a slow and complex process. The book presents a collection of essays by leading experts from various fields, including environmental science, social sciences, and policy-making, to address the multifaceted nature of DRR.</p>
        <p><strong>Contributors:</strong> <span data-field="contributor_1_name">{{ contributor_1_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_1_name">{{ contributor_1_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_1_name">{{ contributor_1_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_1_name">{{ contributor_1_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_1_name">{{ contributor_1_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_1_name">{{ contributor_1_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_1_name">{{ contributor_1_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_1_name">{{ contributor_1_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_1_name">{{ contributor_1_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_1_name">{{ contributor_1_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_1_name">{{ contributor_1_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_1_name">{{ contributor_1_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_1_name">{{ contributor_1_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_1_name">{{ contributor_1_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_1_name">{{ contributor_1_name }}</span></p>
        <p>ISBN: <span data-field="isbn_1">{{ isbn_1 }}</span></p>
        <p>Pages: <span data-field="pages_1">{{ pages_1 }}</span>; Price: <span data-field="price_1">{{ price_1 }}</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Column 2 -->
    <div class="book-entry">
      <img src="placeholder.png" alt="Book Cover" class="book-image">
      <div class="book-details">
        <h3><span data-field="title_2">{{ title_2 }}</span></h3>
        <p>EDITED BY <span data-field="editor_2_name">{{ editor_2_name }}</span></p>
        <p>Climate change adaptation, "building resilience" and "vulnerability and risk reduction" are noble words, but do we really know what is meant by these terms and how to assess them? This book provides a comprehensive overview of the concepts and methodologies used to measure vulnerability to natural hazards, edited by Jörn Birkmann, a leading expert in the field.</p>
        <p><strong>Contents overview:</strong></p>
        <ul class="contents-list">
          <li>Part I: Basic principles and theoretical debates</li>
          <li>Part II: Vulnerability and environmental change</li>
          <li>Part III: Global, national and subnational assessment approaches</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Contributors:</strong> <span data-field="contributor_2_name">{{ contributor_2_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_2_name">{{ contributor_2_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_2_name">{{ contributor_2_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_2_name">{{ contributor_2_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_2_name">{{ contributor_2_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_2_name">{{ contributor_2_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_2_name">{{ contributor_2_name }}</span></p>
        <p>ISBN: <span data-field="isbn_2">{{ isbn_2 }}</span></p>
        <p>Pages: <span data-field="pages_2">{{ pages_2 }}</span>; Price: <span data-field="price_2">{{ price_2 }}</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Column 3 -->
    <div class="book-entry">
      <img src="placeholder.png" alt="Book Cover" class="book-image">
      <div class="book-details">
        <h3><span data-field="title_3">{{ title_3 }}</span></h3>
        <p>EDITED BY <span data-field="editor_3_name">{{ editor_3_name }}</span></p>
        <p>Much of the debate on green growth and environmental governance tends to be general and abstract. This book provides a critical examination of the concepts and theories underlying the green economy and good governance, moving beyond the often-cited, yet sometimes superficial, discussions. It explores the complex interplay between economic development, environmental sustainability, and effective governance structures.</p>
        <p><strong>Contents overview:</strong></p>
        <ul class="contents-list">
          <li>Introduction: Framing the debate on the green economy and governance from different angles.</li>
          <li>Part I: Green economy</li>
          <li>Part II: Governance</li>
          <li>Conclusion</li>
        </ul>
        <p><strong>Contributors:</strong> <span data-field="contributor_3_name">{{ contributor_3_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_3_name">{{ contributor_3_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_3_name">{{ contributor_3_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_3_name">{{ contributor_3_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_3_name">{{ contributor_3_name }}</span>, <span data-field="contributor_3_name">{{ contributor_3_name }}</span></p>
        <p>ISBN: <span data-field="isbn_3">{{ isbn_3 }}</span></p>
        <p>Pages: <span data-field="pages_3">{{ pages_3 }}</span>; Price: <span data-field="price_3">{{ price_3 }}</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="content-grid">
    <!-- Column 1 -->
    <div class="book-entry">
      <img src="placeholder.png" alt="Book Cover" class="book-image">
      <div class="book-details">
        <h3><span data-field="title_4">{{ title_4 }}</span></h3>
        <p>EDITED BY <span data-field="editor_4_name">{{ editor_4_name }}</span>, <span data-field="editor_4_name">{{ editor_4_name }}</span> and <span data-field="editor_4_name">{{ editor_4_name }}</span></p>
        <p>A series of humanitarian tragedies in the 1990s (Somalia, 1992-1994; Rwanda, 1994; Bosnia, 1992-1995) demonstrated the failure of the international community to protect civilians in the context of complex emergencies. These brought to life two fundamental questions: what is the responsibility to protect (R2P) and protection of civilians (PoC)?</p>
        <p><strong>Table of contents:</strong></p>
        <ul class="contents-list">
          <li>The responsibility to protect: Game change and regime change, Hugh Breakey</li>
          <li>The responsibility to protect and the protection of civilians: A view from the United Nations, Angus Francis</li>
          <li>The responsibility to protect and the protection of civilians: A view from the United Nations, Vesselin Popovski</li>
          <li>Peacekeeping, civilian protection mandates and the responsibility to protect, Hitoshi Nasu</li>
          <li>The responsibility to protect and the protection of civilians: A review, Charles Sampford</li>
          <li>Framing a protection service, Annie Herro and Kavitha Sutharathiraj</li>
          <li>The relationship between international humanitarian law and responsibility to protect: From sovereignty to protection, <span data-field="contributor_4_name">{{ contributor_4_name }}</span></li>
          <li>The responsibility to protect civilians from political violence: Locating necessity, <span data-field="contributor_4_name">{{ contributor_4_name }}</span></li>
          <li>The responsibility to protect and the international refugee regime, Angus Francis</li>
          <li>Enhancing the capacities of state and regional institutions in transforming responsibility to protect into action, <span data-field="contributor_4_name">{{ contributor_4_name }}</span></li>
          <li>Towards a "responsibility to provide": Cultivating an ethic of responsible sovereignty in Southeast Asia, <span data-field="contributor_4_name">{{ contributor_4_name }}</span></li>
          <li>Interaction of the norms of protection, Vesselin Popovski</li>
        </ul>
        <p>ISBN: <span data-field="isbn_4">{{ isbn_4 }}</span></p>
        <p>Pages: <span data-field="pages_4">{{ pages_4 }}</span>; Price: <span data-field="price_4">{{ price_4 }}</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Column 2 -->
    <div class="book-entry">
      <img src="placeholder.png" alt="Book Cover" class="book-image">
      <div class="book-details">
        <h3><span data-field="title_5">{{ title_5 }}</span></h3>
        <p>EDITED BY <span data-field="editor_5_name">{{ editor_5_name }}</span> and <span data-field="editor_5_name">{{ editor_5_name }}</span></p>
        <p>Ethics and International Affairs explores the extent and limits of contemporary international ethics and examines the ways in which the international community has responded to some of the most crucial challenges since the end of the Cold War.</p>
        <p>At the centre of the book is a discussion of how responsibility is viewed at individual, national, and international levels. The book also addresses the role of international intervention, environmental issues, considerations of gender, international economic justice, and the role of international law in addressing global problems. The book provides a platform to push for the best implementation and articulation of international ethics, offers focus on the necessity to move beyond abstract moral considerations to concrete action.</p>
        <p><strong>Table of contents:</strong></p>
        <ul class="contents-list">
          <li>Introduction to the second edition: International ethics ten years later: Any progress?</li>
          <li>The ethics of international aid, <span data-field="contributor_5_name">{{ contributor_5_name }}</span></li>
          <li>International law as an approach to international ethics: A plea for a jurisprudential dialogue, <span data-field="contributor_5_name">{{ contributor_5_name }}</span></li>
          <li>The ethics of modern diplomacy, Roberto Toscano</li>
          <li>Violence and ethics: Beyond the reason of state paradigm, Pierre Hassner</li>
          <li>International justice and international order: The case of Bosnia and Kosovo, David Campbell</li>
          <li>Environmental ethics in international society, Oran R. Young</li>
          <li>Ethics, feminism and international affairs, Kimberly Hutchings</li>
          <li>Does globalization have an ethical problem?, Ethan B. Kapstein</li>
          <li>Conclusion: The task(s) of international ethics, Nicholas Rengger</li>
        </ul>
        <p>ISBN: <span data-field="isbn_5">{{ isbn_5 }}</span></p>
        <p>Pages: <span data-field="pages_5">{{ pages_5 }}</span>; Price: <span data-field="price_5">{{ price_5 }}</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Column 3 -->
    <div class="book-entry">
      <img src="placeholder.png" alt="Book Cover" class="book-image">
      <div class="book-details">
        <h3><span data-field="title_6">{{ title_6 }}</span></h3>
        <p>EDITED BY <span data-field="editor_6_name">{{ editor_6_name }}</span></p>
        <p>The concept "rule of law" is well established in domestic constitutions and over many centuries has been used to signify the supremacy of law above the rich and the powerful, above the potential arbitrariness or bias of human decisions.</p>
        <p>This book investigates the concept "international rule of law", which can be a problematic concept. It explores the various dimensions of this concept, including the role of international law, the role of international institutions, and the role of professional ethics in the international arena. It also examines the relationship between international law and professional ethics, particularly in the ethical behaviour of various groups of international actors.</p>
        <p><strong>Table of contents:</strong></p>
        <ul class="contents-list">
          <li>Introduction: Ethical support for the rule of law, Vesselin Popovski</li>
          <li>"Unqualified human good" or a bit of ruling class chatter?, The rule of law at the international level, <span data-field="contributor_6_name">{{ contributor_6_name }}</span></li>
          <li>What is "international temporality"?, Frédéric Mégrét</li>
          <li>Reflections on the rule of law: its significance for North and South as partners in global governance, <span data-field="contributor_6_name">{{ contributor_6_name }}</span></li>
          <li>Professionals without borders: Global ethics and the international rule of law, Charles Sampford</li>
          <li>International civil service ethics, professionalism and the rule of law, Lorne Sosin and Vasudha Sinha</li>
          <li>Judicial ethics at the international criminal tribunals, William Schabas</li>
          <li>International rule of law? Ethics and impartiality of legal professionals in international criminal tribunals, Chandra Lekha Sriram</li>
          <li>Conclusions, Vesselin Popovski</li>
        </ul>
        <p>ISBN: <span data-field="isbn_6">{{ isbn_6 }}</span></p>
        <p>Pages: <span data-field="pages_6">{{ pages_6 }}</span>; Price: <span data-field="price_6">{{ price_6 }}</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

