        <p>"This volume, focusing on children and youth in post-conflict situations, takes a wide array of varied angles, including children's rights, peacebuilding, and the role of youth in post-conflict peacebuilding. Their voices will not be heard unless they can escape the chains of victimhood and their agency in post-war recovery effort is recognized."</p>
        <p>By drawing on experiences from post-conflict environments in different parts of the world, this volume examines the challenges and opportunities for children and youth in post-conflict settings, and the ways in which they can be empowered to protect and empower children and youth in post-conflict environments. The volume also examines the role of youth in peacebuilding and the ways in which they can be involved in the process of peacebuilding and the ways in which they can be involved in the process of peacebuilding and the ways in which they can be involved in the process of peacebuilding.</p>
